ox": {"x": 1331.4, "y": 1329.3, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 27.200000000000045}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.976", "bbox": {"x": 1334.7, "y": 1376.8, "width": 51.0, "height": 20.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.803", "bbox": {"x": 1436.6, "y": 1285.1, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 20.40000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.813", "bbox": {"x": 1436.6, "y": 1332.4, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 17.299999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.887", "bbox": {"x": 1436.6, "y": 1376.4, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 21.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.976", "bbox": {"x": 1331.4, "y": 1424.5, "width": 54.299999999999955, "height": 23.799999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.977", "bbox": {"x": 1331.4, "y": 1468.4, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 28.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.940", "bbox": {"x": 1334.7, "y": 1516.3, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 20.40000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.887", "bbox": {"x": 1436.6, "y": 1424.4, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 20.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.871", "bbox": {"x": 1436.6, "y": 1472.1, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 17.299999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.793", "bbox": {"x": 1436.6, "y": 1516.3, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 20.40000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.943", "bbox": {"x": 1334.7, "y": 1563.9, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 20.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.803", "bbox": {"x": 1436.6, "y": 1563.9, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 20.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.928", "bbox": {"x": 1334.7, "y": 1611.3, "width": 50.90000000000009, "height": 17.09999999999991}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.785", "bbox": {"x": 1440.0, "y": 1611.3, "width": 47.5, "height": 17.09999999999991}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "combining LM and Graph Contrastive Learning (GCL) to incorporate relational information. The visualization results in Figure 3 reveal notable differences between the two configurations. Embeddings generated solely with Language Models (LM) showed less distinct clustering, with considerable overlap between the two groups. This overlap suggests a limited ability to distinguish drugs that interact with the selected protein from those that do not. In contrast, embeddings produced using our proposed method, which integrates LM with Graph Contrastive Learning (GCL), exhibited tighter clustering and more pronounced separation.", "bbox": {"x": 842.3, "y": 1761.0, "width": 675.9000000000001, "height": 360.4000000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Frontiers in Systems Biology", "bbox": {"x": 135.9, "y": 2226.8, "width": 258.1, "height": 20.40000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "10", "bbox": {"x": 811.7, "y": 2226.8, "width": 27.200000000000045, "height": 17.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "frontiersin.org", "bbox": {"x": 1382.3, "y": 2226.8, "width": 135.9000000000001, "height": 20.40000000000009}}], "ms": 262.86}